WEBVTT

00:00:04.230 --> 00:00:07.980
When it's a lucky day with nice weather

00:00:07.980 --> 00:00:11.770
I hope we have a good time together

00:00:11.690 --> 00:00:19.240
Nekogami Yaoyorozu

00:00:11.690 --> 00:00:19.240
FFFpeeps presents

00:00:11.770 --> 00:00:15.620
Today let's keep

00:00:17.340 --> 00:00:19.240
Sharing laughs

00:00:19.690 --> 00:00:26.670
You take care of my true wishes in secret

00:00:27.110 --> 00:00:34.220
You always cheer me up after bad days

00:00:34.220 --> 00:00:40.580
I'm sure everyone has known it since childhood

00:00:40.980 --> 00:00:49.250
You pretend you don't care, but you're always a good friend

00:00:50.400 --> 00:00:58.650
You have another busy day as a god; you just can't help but help out others

00:00:58.650 --> 00:01:04.990
Everyone is cheered up by your love

00:01:05.380 --> 00:01:13.300
I love always being together while you help others

00:01:13.300 --> 00:01:20.820
I'll protect that precious smile; you know what I mean

00:01:21.060 --> 00:01:24.820
When it's a lucky day with nice weather

00:01:24.820 --> 00:01:28.400
We should go visit the shrine together

00:01:44.350 --> 00:01:45.620
Here it goes.

00:01:49.000 --> 00:01:50.330
Now, place your bet!

00:01:51.270 --> 00:01:52.750
Evens or odds?

00:01:55.460 --> 00:01:57.710
So far, the numbers have been...

00:01:57.710 --> 00:01:59.330
5-2, odd;

00:01:59.330 --> 00:02:00.880
4-6, even;

00:02:00.880 --> 00:02:02.480
1-1, even;

00:02:02.480 --> 00:02:04.110
2-6, even.

00:02:04.110 --> 00:02:09.540
It's been been evens three times in a
row, so I doubt it'll be evens again.

00:02:09.540 --> 00:02:13.260
Wait, it could be that evens have the momentum.

00:02:13.260 --> 00:02:15.900
Now, what do you choose?

00:02:15.900 --> 00:02:19.490
Evens or odds, those are your only choices.

00:02:19.490 --> 00:02:22.280
I've made up my mind! It must be odds!

00:02:22.280 --> 00:02:25.480
I bet the rest of my game pieces on odds!

00:02:25.480 --> 00:02:26.990
Odds? Very well.

00:02:26.990 --> 00:02:27.540
Then...

00:02:27.540 --> 00:02:28.810
Let's see it!

00:02:28.810 --> 00:02:29.790
1-1, even!

00:02:33.030 --> 00:02:35.650
Okay, those are all mine now!

00:02:37.530 --> 00:02:39.370
I shouldn't have done that!

00:02:39.370 --> 00:02:43.180
Donation money from your
shabby shrine isn't enough, is it?

00:02:44.740 --> 00:02:47.260
My entire savings that I had built up little by little!

00:02:47.260 --> 00:02:51.390
Oh well, I'll just take this old-looking game, then.

00:02:57.430 --> 00:03:00.100
Anything but that video game!

00:03:00.100 --> 00:03:08.300
That has a save file with a Level 99 Kabra's Blade and a Level 99 Spiral Wind Demon that I've slaved over for a year with painstaking care!

00:03:08.300 --> 00:03:10.200
Let me reiterate!

00:03:10.200 --> 00:03:15.620
That game has a save file with a Level 99
Kabra's Blade and a Level 99 Spiral—

00:03:15.620 --> 00:03:17.620
Like I care!

00:03:17.620 --> 00:03:21.620
Shizuha, I'm sure you're human
enough to have compassion—

00:03:21.620 --> 00:03:24.880
Let me go! Give up already!

00:03:24.880 --> 00:03:28.880
A cat shouldn't be begging
a fox for human compassion!

00:03:32.890 --> 00:03:37.770
If you're frustrated, come and try to get
it back after you've made some cash.

00:03:39.630 --> 00:03:41.390
She's a devil!

00:03:49.070 --> 00:03:51.630
Oh, Shizuha-sama, are you already leav—

00:03:51.630 --> 00:03:53.630
Yuzu-chan!

00:03:53.630 --> 00:03:57.380
Yuzu-chan, you're so cute and
hardworking every time I see you!

00:03:57.380 --> 00:04:00.760
I hope you'll become Gonta's bride soon!

00:04:00.760 --> 00:04:02.470
Oh...

00:04:02.470 --> 00:04:03.720
Oh, right.

00:04:03.720 --> 00:04:07.140
Here's some donation money I hustled out of Mayu.

00:04:07.140 --> 00:04:09.440
Use it to feed her or something.

00:04:09.440 --> 00:04:11.150
Oh, thank you.

00:04:11.150 --> 00:04:13.190
Just don't give it back to her, okay?

00:04:13.190 --> 00:04:15.780
She'll waste it on something useless if you do.

00:04:15.780 --> 00:04:17.430
Got it.

00:04:21.560 --> 00:04:25.480
Now, what should I do about this?

00:04:31.080 --> 00:04:32.530
Wham wham!

00:04:32.540 --> 00:04:34.920
We've got delicious nam pla!

00:04:34.920 --> 00:04:36.660
Yay!

00:04:48.420 --> 00:04:51.100
Nam pla is the best!

00:04:52.710 --> 00:04:55.940
Nam pla ramen was a big success!

00:04:55.940 --> 00:05:01.060
At last, I've managed to open a fabulous store!

00:05:04.100 --> 00:05:08.560
President, let's keep expanding and aim for the top!

00:05:08.560 --> 00:05:09.860
Of course!

00:05:11.440 --> 00:05:14.420
Huff, huff! Chuff, chuff!

00:05:14.420 --> 00:05:16.910
You look very excited, President!

00:05:16.910 --> 00:05:20.280
This alluring scent, the scent of nam pla!

00:05:22.180 --> 00:05:25.680
This ramen smells too fishy.

00:05:25.680 --> 00:05:28.430
What was that? You need more nam pla?

00:05:32.440 --> 00:05:38.190
You made it even worse!
I can't eat this anymore!

00:05:38.190 --> 00:05:42.700
Go, go, nam pla! C'mon, c'mon, nam pla!

00:05:42.700 --> 00:05:45.200
Go, go, nam pla!

00:05:43.350 --> 00:05:45.200
They aren't listening.

00:05:45.200 --> 00:05:47.580
C'mon, c'mon, nam pla!

00:05:48.790 --> 00:05:50.580
My treasure...

00:05:50.580 --> 00:05:54.190
I want to get it back, but I have no money.

00:05:57.700 --> 00:06:02.380
She isn't known in the heavens as the
"Hardheaded Female Paladin" for nothing.

00:06:02.380 --> 00:06:09.040
She'll go and sell my magnum opus
of a year of gaming for dirt cheap!

00:06:09.920 --> 00:06:11.380
Wait a sec!

00:06:11.380 --> 00:06:13.400
Selling it isn't <i>that bad.</i>

00:06:13.400 --> 00:06:19.050
I'm willing to give it up if the game would
end up in a fellow gamer's possession.

00:06:19.050 --> 00:06:22.740
However, it might be left to collect dust,

00:06:24.070 --> 00:06:25.240
or even...

00:06:24.480 --> 00:06:25.240
I don't need this.

00:06:25.240 --> 00:06:27.730
dumped on a random road...

00:06:27.730 --> 00:06:28.950
Tada.

00:06:28.950 --> 00:06:30.730
left to fall apart...

00:06:33.440 --> 00:06:35.000
I can't waste time like this!

00:06:35.000 --> 00:06:36.880
I will get it back at all costs!

00:06:37.880 --> 00:06:42.630
I am a cat god: a guardian of forgotten items and memories.

00:06:44.410 --> 00:06:46.680
Hark, oh my beloved game software,

00:06:46.680 --> 00:06:49.080
thine master commands ye! Reveal to me your location!

00:06:53.340 --> 00:06:55.200
Yo, Gonta.

00:06:57.000 --> 00:06:58.670
I'm right here.

00:06:58.670 --> 00:07:01.540
M-Mother! What brings you here?

00:07:01.540 --> 00:07:07.640
Do I need a reason for coming to see my son?

00:07:07.640 --> 00:07:10.990
Oh, that's right. You like video games, don't you?

00:07:10.990 --> 00:07:12.200
You can keep this.

00:07:12.200 --> 00:07:13.190
Th-Thanks.

00:07:13.200 --> 00:07:15.700
What's she up to?

00:07:15.700 --> 00:07:18.950
I think I already have this one.

00:07:18.950 --> 00:07:21.330
Hm, is someone here?

00:07:21.330 --> 00:07:26.960
The Cherry Blossom God, Shoudou-san, is here to discuss when the cherry blossoms should bloom next year.

00:07:28.360 --> 00:07:31.720
His granddaughter, Yoshino-san,
should be coming by a bit later.

00:07:31.720 --> 00:07:35.880
Then, before that clueless girl gets here...

00:07:35.880 --> 00:07:36.340
Sorry?

00:07:36.340 --> 00:07:44.100
TL Note: Chinchirorin is a dice game similar to Cee-lo.

00:07:36.340 --> 00:07:40.970
That Cherry Blossom God is a fool for a game of chinchirorin.

00:07:40.970 --> 00:07:44.100
It's my chance to make some money.

00:07:44.100 --> 00:07:48.770
Mother, please don't get in the way of my work!

00:07:48.770 --> 00:07:50.150
What's the problem?

00:07:50.150 --> 00:07:54.490
Playing dice is a Japanese tradition
that dates back to the Heian period.

00:07:50.150 --> 00:08:09.490
TL Note: <i>Me ga/no deru</i> can literally mean either "to sprout" or "for a number on a die to come up," and in either case, the secondary figurative meaning is "to have good luck."

00:07:54.490 --> 00:08:03.000
Dice are sometimes offered to shrines as symbols of good luck, so us gods are quite involved with them as well.

00:08:03.000 --> 00:08:06.500
Still, it's kind of...

00:08:06.500 --> 00:08:09.490
Gonta, bring us some sake and fish.

00:08:09.500 --> 00:08:11.110
I'm counting on you!

00:08:22.500 --> 00:08:23.830
I would rather not.

00:08:23.830 --> 00:08:32.160
Don't be ridiculous! Are you saying you're fine with my lovely, precious video game being left in the rain to eventually fall to pieces?

00:08:32.160 --> 00:08:35.540
That's just your imagination, Mayu-sama.

00:08:40.210 --> 00:08:43.460
Yuzu, you're heartless.

00:08:43.460 --> 00:08:50.380
You can't understand the pain of children you've dearly raised being taken away.

00:08:50.380 --> 00:08:52.880
No, you don't!

00:08:52.880 --> 00:08:58.870
But you shouldn't secretly take back something you've bet and lost. That'd make you a thief.

00:08:58.870 --> 00:09:01.850
I'm not secretly taking it back!

00:09:01.850 --> 00:09:05.920
I'll get it back through a friendly negotiation.

00:09:05.920 --> 00:09:07.920
Please, Yuzu!

00:09:08.030 --> 00:09:09.200
I'm begging you!

00:09:09.810 --> 00:09:12.670
Well, I guess I have no choice.

00:09:12.670 --> 00:09:14.680
I did it!

00:09:14.680 --> 00:09:21.020
If Mother starts drinking liquor this early, she'll end up
drinking through the whole day. This should be enough.

00:09:22.040 --> 00:09:23.630
I wonder who it is?

00:09:23.640 --> 00:09:25.560
Yes, I'm coming!

00:09:25.560 --> 00:09:27.130
Comin—

00:09:29.920 --> 00:09:33.190
Y-Y-Yu...

00:09:33.190 --> 00:09:33.950
Yuzu-san!

00:09:33.950 --> 00:09:36.450
Did you come here to see me?

00:09:36.450 --> 00:09:39.200
O-Oh, no... um...

00:09:39.200 --> 00:09:42.060
We're here for part-time work.

00:09:42.060 --> 00:09:45.420
Part-time work? Oh, you came along?

00:09:47.110 --> 00:09:48.940
I shouldn't get angry.

00:09:48.940 --> 00:09:53.110
Well, didn't you say you'd like
some help with the shrine work?

00:09:53.110 --> 00:09:57.840
We both came over to give you a hand.

00:09:57.840 --> 00:10:01.850
Yuzu-san wants part-time work at this shrine...

00:10:01.850 --> 00:10:03.340
You're hired!

00:10:09.920 --> 00:10:11.110
How is it?

00:10:11.110 --> 00:10:14.090
This is awesome!

00:10:14.090 --> 00:10:17.610
Jeez, thank goodness he's an idiot.

00:10:17.610 --> 00:10:23.100
Now then, what should I ask
you to do? What should I ask?

00:10:23.100 --> 00:10:24.750
Oh, that's right!

00:10:24.750 --> 00:10:27.650
I'd like you to tidy up the shed.

00:10:27.650 --> 00:10:30.320
Now, please come here!

00:10:30.320 --> 00:10:31.500
Okay...

00:10:31.500 --> 00:10:36.200
S-So, Gonta, what should I be doing?

00:10:36.200 --> 00:10:39.140
You go over there and start sweeping.

00:10:39.340 --> 00:10:43.840
D-Damn him! He's getting carried away!

00:10:44.140 --> 00:10:46.640
Now, Yuzu-san, this way, please.

00:10:46.640 --> 00:10:49.250
That actually makes things easier for me.

00:10:49.250 --> 00:10:52.230
This is my chance to look for the game.

00:10:53.870 --> 00:10:56.120
Yuzu, forgive me!

00:10:56.130 --> 00:11:01.980
I know I can't manage a friendly negotiation with Shizuha, the Hardheaded Female Paladin!

00:11:01.980 --> 00:11:05.850
My plan's always been to secretly and
stealthily get it back without asking!

00:11:05.850 --> 00:11:07.670
Yes, it has!

00:11:10.580 --> 00:11:14.670
If Yuzu and I were dice, would we come up evens or odds?

00:11:15.680 --> 00:11:18.620
Over here, Yuzu-san! This is the shed.

00:11:18.630 --> 00:11:21.050
It's kind of messy, just like you'd expect from a shed—

00:11:22.050 --> 00:11:25.620
Are you all right, Gonta-san? That was a nice sound.

00:11:25.620 --> 00:11:29.440
This drum came in handy during the festival this year.

00:11:30.440 --> 00:11:34.740
I want the items on this shelf sorted into these boxes.

00:11:34.990 --> 00:11:36.720
Got it.

00:11:36.720 --> 00:11:38.510
We'll do it together.

00:11:38.510 --> 00:11:39.240
Sure!

00:11:40.040 --> 00:11:43.600
All right, I'll put books into this box.

00:11:48.150 --> 00:11:50.150
Yuzu-san!

00:11:51.250 --> 00:11:53.340
She's so pretty.

00:11:56.250 --> 00:11:57.670
Y-Yuzu-san...

00:11:57.670 --> 00:11:58.350
Yes?

00:11:58.360 --> 00:12:01.090
U-Um, are you tired?

00:12:01.090 --> 00:12:02.990
We just started.

00:12:02.990 --> 00:12:04.930
R-Right...

00:12:05.720 --> 00:12:08.640
Come on! Get a grip, Gonta! You're a man!

00:12:09.230 --> 00:12:13.190
Yuzu-san, you look very nice in that shrine maiden outfit.

00:12:13.190 --> 00:12:16.150
But you'd look the best...

00:12:16.450 --> 00:12:18.450
in a white...

00:12:18.450 --> 00:12:20.560
wedding dress!

00:12:23.310 --> 00:12:25.850
G-Gonta-san, are you...

00:12:25.850 --> 00:12:28.160
I'm proposing to you.

00:12:28.560 --> 00:12:30.810
I'm so happy!

00:12:30.810 --> 00:12:32.820
As am I.

00:12:34.980 --> 00:12:36.940
Wait up!

00:12:38.920 --> 00:12:40.200
Oh, it slipped.

00:12:40.210 --> 00:12:41.670
Slipped?!

00:12:42.780 --> 00:12:44.620
Oh, the book.

00:12:44.620 --> 00:12:45.300
Um...

00:12:45.300 --> 00:12:50.960
Oh... ah... yes. The book slipped, didn't it? That was dangerous. This book is thick.

00:12:50.960 --> 00:12:52.290
Here you go.

00:12:53.340 --> 00:12:54.560
Oh, that was dangerous.

00:12:56.260 --> 00:12:58.470
It makes this "bam" sound. It's a drum after all.

00:12:58.470 --> 00:13:00.070
Oh you!

00:13:03.620 --> 00:13:04.680
Not here!

00:13:04.680 --> 00:13:06.150
Not here, not here!

00:13:08.570 --> 00:13:11.310
My powers told me it was in this shrine, though.

00:13:11.310 --> 00:13:12.710
Mayu-sama!

00:13:13.510 --> 00:13:14.820
Oh, Yoshino!

00:13:14.820 --> 00:13:15.900
Yes, it's me, Yoshino!

00:13:15.900 --> 00:13:17.960
Mayu-sama, why are you here?

00:13:17.960 --> 00:13:20.780
And why are you in that dress?

00:13:20.780 --> 00:13:22.760
I-I'm just working part-time.

00:13:22.760 --> 00:13:28.720
Gonta begged me to help, so I came
here with Yuzu to give him a hand.

00:13:28.720 --> 00:13:34.230
Oh, that's right! Yuzu looks quite
splendid in her shrine maiden outfit!

00:13:34.230 --> 00:13:36.560
I want to see it!

00:13:36.560 --> 00:13:40.230
She's cleaning up the shed with Gonta,
so why don't you go see her there?

00:13:40.230 --> 00:13:41.980
I'll go, then!

00:13:41.980 --> 00:13:46.240
And I'll look for my game while everyone's in the shed!

00:13:52.490 --> 00:13:54.000
Yuzu-san!

00:13:54.000 --> 00:13:55.020
Yes!

00:13:55.020 --> 00:13:56.480
Isn't it hot?

00:13:56.480 --> 00:13:59.650
It isn't hot at all.

00:13:59.650 --> 00:14:00.670
Yuzu-san!

00:14:00.670 --> 00:14:01.250
Yes?

00:14:01.250 --> 00:14:03.750
Aren't you thirsty?

00:14:03.760 --> 00:14:08.130
Thank you, but I'm doing just fine.

00:14:08.140 --> 00:14:10.410
Yuzu-san and me...

00:14:12.670 --> 00:14:15.310
The two of us are taking on the task together...

00:14:15.310 --> 00:14:18.900
We're getting closer and closer!

00:14:23.950 --> 00:14:25.040
Yuzu-san!

00:14:25.040 --> 00:14:26.160
Yes!

00:14:26.160 --> 00:14:28.680
Yuzu-san, I lo—

00:14:28.080 --> 00:14:30.180
Hello!

00:14:30.180 --> 00:14:31.210
Yoshino-san!

00:14:31.210 --> 00:14:35.560
I heard you looked wonderful in a shrine
maiden outfit, so I'm here to see it!

00:14:35.560 --> 00:14:38.770
Wonderful? Oh my, I'm flattered.

00:14:38.770 --> 00:14:39.440
Oh, it slipped.

00:14:39.440 --> 00:14:42.140
Slipped?!

00:14:42.150 --> 00:14:43.950
Oh, the box.

00:14:43.950 --> 00:14:47.660
Ah, I'm sorry I keep dropping things.

00:14:47.660 --> 00:14:50.700
Oh, not at all! Don't worry about it!

00:14:50.700 --> 00:14:52.710
Now, let's keep going!

00:14:52.710 --> 00:14:54.960
Oh, sure.

00:14:56.780 --> 00:15:01.200
Jeez, this place is so big I can't find it.

00:15:03.210 --> 00:15:04.480
I feel it!

00:15:05.290 --> 00:15:06.540
I should be right this time!

00:15:10.420 --> 00:15:12.670
F-Found it!

00:15:12.670 --> 00:15:15.680
That stain, that scratch!

00:15:16.290 --> 00:15:18.910
There's no mistaking it.

00:15:18.910 --> 00:15:22.350
My divine senses are on an entirely different—

00:15:22.360 --> 00:15:25.440
Junmai brew is the best!

00:15:24.210 --> 00:15:25.440
Sh-Shizuha!

00:15:25.590 --> 00:15:27.710
At this rate...

00:15:30.190 --> 00:15:31.190
This is bad!

00:15:31.190 --> 00:15:33.430
I have to hurry up and hide!

00:15:33.430 --> 00:15:35.310
What should I do?

00:15:35.310 --> 00:15:36.160
Oh well!

00:15:36.160 --> 00:15:37.560
Summon!

00:15:40.700 --> 00:15:46.360
I told Gonta to bring fish and sake, but he never did.

00:15:46.360 --> 00:15:50.670
Things just don't get exciting without you.

00:15:55.460 --> 00:15:56.550
What is that?

00:15:56.550 --> 00:16:00.050
There shouldn't be a cardboard box here.

00:16:00.060 --> 00:16:03.300
The more I look at it, the more suspicious it gets.

00:16:05.130 --> 00:16:06.230
This is painful!

00:16:06.230 --> 00:16:07.810
Get going already!

00:16:07.810 --> 00:16:13.230
Well, whatever, I should hurry back
and enjoy drinking with that old man.

00:16:14.600 --> 00:16:17.700
Chinchirorin's getting kind of boring.

00:16:17.700 --> 00:16:21.450
Maybe I'll use crooked dice and wrap it up.

00:16:21.450 --> 00:16:24.660
What's that?! Crooked dice?!

00:16:29.210 --> 00:16:30.710
I see now!

00:16:35.090 --> 00:16:38.080
So that's what it was.

00:16:39.870 --> 00:16:41.390
Hold it right there!

00:16:41.390 --> 00:16:43.390
Is that Mayu?

00:16:44.560 --> 00:16:47.390
I heard what you just said.

00:16:47.390 --> 00:16:49.590
You look dumb.

00:16:49.600 --> 00:16:53.230
Why are wearing a shrine maiden outfit
and have a cardboard box on your head?

00:16:53.230 --> 00:16:57.320
Silence! That doesn't matter!

00:16:57.320 --> 00:17:00.650
You have cheated in the game with me!

00:17:00.660 --> 00:17:04.160
Those crooked dice in your hand are the undeniable proof!

00:17:04.160 --> 00:17:07.580
What's going on over there?

00:17:07.580 --> 00:17:09.920
Mother, did you do something?

00:17:09.920 --> 00:17:15.960
Oh, you're all here. This woman cheated at dice!

00:17:21.290 --> 00:17:25.580
This is amazing! Only 1's come up even
though there are other numbers!

00:17:25.580 --> 00:17:27.230
That's dirty.

00:17:29.250 --> 00:17:32.480
It does seem they're crooked dice.

00:17:32.480 --> 00:17:38.050
How's that? Are you still going to play innocent?

00:17:38.050 --> 00:17:48.370
They might be crooked dice, but you can't prove I used it in the game we played, can you?

00:17:48.370 --> 00:17:54.070
I see. You do have a point.

00:17:54.070 --> 00:17:58.880
However, that won't satisfy Mayu-sama.

00:17:58.880 --> 00:18:06.890
How about this, you two: settle grudges
from gambling through gambling!

00:18:08.930 --> 00:18:12.400
It'll be decided in a single round of evens-or-odds!

00:18:12.400 --> 00:18:19.300
Mayu-sama will roll the dice I prepared. Is that okay?

00:18:20.850 --> 00:18:22.400
Yes.

00:18:23.410 --> 00:18:25.110
Here I go, Shizuha.

00:18:25.110 --> 00:18:27.100
I'm ready.

00:18:28.110 --> 00:18:29.440
Here it goes.

00:18:33.530 --> 00:18:36.440
Now, evens or odds?

00:18:36.440 --> 00:18:38.200
It's one of the two.

00:18:42.280 --> 00:18:44.050
What a foolish lass.

00:18:44.050 --> 00:18:53.400
I don't know if you were trying to take
revenge, but I clearly saw you swap the dice.

00:18:53.900 --> 00:18:57.400
The crooked dice are inside the cup.

00:18:57.400 --> 00:18:59.630
That means...

00:18:59.630 --> 00:19:01.760
Evens!

00:19:01.760 --> 00:19:04.610
You lose again, Mayu.

00:19:04.610 --> 00:19:07.290
You're set on evens, correct?

00:19:07.290 --> 00:19:11.000
Of course. Now hurry up and open it.

00:19:11.000 --> 00:19:13.860
Very well.

00:19:13.870 --> 00:19:15.040
Let's see it!

00:19:16.170 --> 00:19:17.750
3-6, odd!

00:19:17.750 --> 00:19:21.260
How's that?! I win!

00:19:21.260 --> 00:19:23.990
Wh-What?! Impossible!

00:19:23.990 --> 00:19:27.100
I clearly saw her swap the dice!

00:19:27.300 --> 00:19:31.330
Mayu, didn't you use my crooked dice just now?

00:19:31.330 --> 00:19:32.520
Crooked dice?

00:19:32.520 --> 00:19:35.770
Hmph, are you talking about these?

00:19:37.170 --> 00:19:38.270
Th-Then...

00:19:38.270 --> 00:19:47.530
You had the crooked dice at first and then you swapped them with the straight dice?

00:19:47.530 --> 00:19:51.540
That's why I told you it's one of the two.

00:19:51.540 --> 00:19:55.230
Then you just took your chances?!

00:19:55.230 --> 00:19:57.830
What if you had rolled evens?

00:19:57.830 --> 00:20:00.710
I'd have dealt with it somehow.

00:20:00.710 --> 00:20:07.300
I won't cheat to get back a game
I treasure like my own child.

00:20:08.300 --> 00:20:09.180
Gonta.

00:20:09.300 --> 00:20:10.390
Yes!

00:20:10.390 --> 00:20:14.390
Give this one back to Mayu.

00:20:14.390 --> 00:20:15.710
Yes!

00:20:15.710 --> 00:20:19.010
I definitely saw this game before somewhere.

00:20:19.010 --> 00:20:20.470
Oh, I remember now!

00:20:20.480 --> 00:20:21.400
What is it, Gonta?

00:20:21.400 --> 00:20:25.760
I lent Mayu this game over a year ago.

00:20:25.760 --> 00:20:27.200
This stain and this scratch...

00:20:29.930 --> 00:20:31.390
Oh, you're right!

00:20:32.980 --> 00:20:35.290
Whatever, you can keep it.

00:20:35.290 --> 00:20:37.240
Really?!

00:20:37.240 --> 00:20:40.790
You're such a nice guy!

00:20:41.490 --> 00:20:45.700
My Kabra's Blade and Spiral Wind Demon!

00:20:45.700 --> 00:20:50.050
Let's continue our journey!

00:20:50.050 --> 00:20:53.340
Huh, I think I forgot something.

00:20:53.350 --> 00:20:59.720
I'm glad for you, Gonta. Yuzu came all the way over to prepare for a bride's life.

00:20:59.720 --> 00:21:02.720
Oh, Mother, she's just here to work part-time.

00:21:02.720 --> 00:21:03.520
...for now.

00:21:03.530 --> 00:21:05.340
Just kidding!

00:21:05.340 --> 00:21:08.610
Why am I staying here?

00:21:08.610 --> 00:21:10.120
Oh, Yuzu, it slipped.

00:21:10.120 --> 00:21:12.030
Slipped?!

00:21:12.030 --> 00:21:13.320
Oh, the taro.

00:21:13.320 --> 00:21:18.740
Come on, why do I never get
the real nip slips I want to see?!

00:21:18.740 --> 00:21:21.700
Jeez!

00:21:21.700 --> 00:21:25.760
Slips! Slips! Slips!

00:21:26.160 --> 00:21:29.760
I'm sorry. These taros are always so slippery.

00:21:29.760 --> 00:21:34.250
Yeah, definitely! Warmed sake is so amazing!

00:21:34.260 --> 00:21:35.470
I see.

00:21:35.670 --> 00:21:41.480
But really... when should I leave?

00:21:44.530 --> 00:21:48.370
This game is as addicting as ever!

00:21:48.370 --> 00:21:50.870
But I'm getting hungry.

00:21:50.870 --> 00:21:55.310
Hey, Yuzu, is the dinner ready yet? Yuzu?

00:22:02.140 --> 00:22:09.190
I gently peered into the future which we call tomorrow

00:22:09.190 --> 00:22:13.320
Looking at the world upside down

00:22:13.360 --> 00:22:20.360
I projected my memories upon the glittering cotton candy clouds

00:22:20.360 --> 00:22:24.490
And hung rainbow ribbons

00:22:24.490 --> 00:22:31.790
When I'm left alone, I feel lonely and depressed

00:22:32.210 --> 00:22:38.260
So stay here forever

00:22:38.260 --> 00:22:43.510
I'm sure everyone has some

00:22:43.510 --> 00:22:49.430
Unfulfilled desires locked inside their hearts

00:22:51.690 --> 00:23:01.610
I want you to realize that small memory that won't disappear is the key. Yeah

00:23:01.610 --> 00:23:08.080
You're always the only one

00:23:08.080 --> 00:23:12.370
Who can make me reminisce fondly

00:23:26.400 --> 00:23:41.370
Next Episode

00:23:27.200 --> 00:23:29.680
I'm bored. I wonder if anyone's coming over.

00:23:29.680 --> 00:23:30.930
Mayu-sama, let's play cards!

00:23:30.930 --> 00:23:34.680
Oh, Yoshino, how about I
tell you a short ghost story?

00:23:34.680 --> 00:23:36.560
No! Why?

00:23:36.560 --> 00:23:39.480
Is that the story of when you first came here?

00:23:38.410 --> 00:23:41.370
Rainy Rainy

00:23:39.480 --> 00:23:41.400
Yuzu, you're sharp.
